Another wild guess:
Repeatedly I found "configure" checks to fail because
the test procedures sometimes create "conftest" as a file,
and sometimes as a directory. To get rid of it,
"rm -f" may not be enough, a "rm -rf" might be necessary,
so change the script(s) accordingly.
That was on HP-UX, but might apply to Tru64 as well.



